From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:53:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Bound session reconnect attempts and exclude legacy
 write replay

Pass the remaining reconnect window into every attempt and recompute it after the snapshot before dispatching PATCH/DELETE. Preserve the 30s per-hop cap and never send zero/unlimited after expiry. Mark identity-less legacy failures non-replayable while preserving their cause and message.

Proof: six new regression cases fail on the original code (86s snapshot/reconnect window; repeated identity-less DELETE). GREEN: 66 vitest tests across five session consumer suites; five guard/timeout mutants killed; Desktop tsc and touched-file eslint pass; scripts/check --base origin/main passes. The transport still owns cancellation; JS scheduling is not a hard real-time guarantee.
